#: ../../../contributing/index.md:0
msgid ""
"Contribute to the snap documentation by reporting issues and submitting pull "
"requests for corrections, clarifications, and technical improvements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:8
msgid "Contribute to our docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:10
msgid ""
"Our documentation is a community effort, published on [snapcraft.io/docs]"
"(https://snapcraft.io/docs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:12
msgid ""
"**We warmly welcome community contributions, suggestions, fixes and "
"constructive feedback.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:14
msgid ""
"Contributing to documentation can be a fantastic way to get started as a "
"contributor to open source projects, no matter your level of experience!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:16
msgid ""
"We hope to make it as easy as possible to contribute. If you need help at "
"all with the contribution process, please let us know!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:18
msgid "Contributions we accept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:20
msgid ""
"We especially value contributions that improve the documentation's clarity, "
"accuracy, and usefulness. If you spot a problem, you can report it to us "
"using the \"Give feedback\" button at the top of every documentation page. "
"Please give us as much information as you can to help us address the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:25
msgid ""
"If the issue is one of the following very small issues, and you want to fix "
"it yourself, you can submit a pull request (PR) with your changes directly "
"in the [GitHub web interface](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/"
"working-with-files/managing-files/editing-files):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:29
msgid "Typo corrections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:30
msgid "Minor technical corrections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:31
msgid "Broken link fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:32
msgid "Small clarifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:34
msgid ""
"For changes larger than those, we require contributor PRs to be tied to an "
"issue. Examples of changes that require an issue are things like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:37
msgid "Adding new sections or pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:38
msgid "Restructuring existing pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:39
msgid "Extensive rewording"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:40
msgid "Significant technical corrections or updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:41
msgid "Feature additions or enhancements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:43
msgid "Contributions we don't accept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:45
msgid ""
"We reserve the right to reject any contribution at our own discretion where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:47
msgid ""
"**The outline of proposed work has not already been agreed by a maintainer.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:48
msgid ""
"A PR must be tied to a valid and agreed issue unless it only makes a small "
"change. Submitting an issue after a PR doesn't *guarantee* that we will then "
"accept the PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:50
msgid "**The pull request far exceeds the scope of what was agreed.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:51
msgid ""
"\"Scope creep\" makes it much harder to review and accept changes. If a pull "
"request becomes too large, we may ask you to break it into multiple smaller "
"PRs. Stick to the scope of the original issue as much as you can -- if you "
"discover more changes need to be made, discuss them in the PR or the "
"original issue. A new PR can be submitted with the extra fixes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:53
msgid "**The contribution makes changes without value.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:54
msgid ""
"To have value, changes must be a *specific and concrete improvement* over "
"what already exists. We don't accept generic \"polishing\" (e.g. "
"substituting synonyms, rewording without adding clarity). If your "
"contribution contains *some* of these, we will ask you to undo them -- but "
"will gladly accept the remaining parts of your pull request that are real "
"improvements. If your contribution *only* contains low-value changes, it "
"will be rejected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:56
msgid "**We deem the contribution to be AI generated.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:57
msgid ""
"We don't want any part of our documentation to look or feel like it was "
"produced by AI. Therefore, if what you submitted cannot be easily "
"distinguished from AI output, it does not meet our contribution requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:59
msgid ""
"**The issue the pull request is addressing was assigned to someone else.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:60
msgid ""
"We want to make this a safe place for contributors to work on issues. Please "
"treat others as you'd want to be treated. If you like an issue someone else "
"is working on, let us know and we'll create a similar one for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:62
msgid "The Open Documentation Academy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:64
msgid ""
"The SnapD project is a proud member of the [Canonical Open Documentation "
"Academy](https://documentation.academy/) (CODA). If you are new to making "
"open source contributions, or new to technical writing and want to boost "
"your skills -- or both! -- we will be glad to help. You can find open issues "
"on the [CODA dashboard](https://canonical.github.io/coda-dashboard/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:69
msgid "AI policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:71
msgid ""
"The SnapD documentation has been created by humans, for humans. The "
"occasional \"jagged edges\" you might find (typos, slightly unconventional "
"wording, humour) represent the very human voices of the people who "
"collaborated to create it. We don't want to average those away by passing "
"the documentation through LLMs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:74
msgid ""
"This policy exists to protect our readers, our community of contributors, "
"and the project maintainers. As AI continues to evolve, we will update these "
"guidelines accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:78
msgid "Acceptable use of AI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:80
msgid ""
"We don't ban our contributors from using AI. However, we do expect anyone "
"contributing to this project to use it responsibly, as a helper, and not as "
"something that replaces them. Some examples of acceptable usage include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:82
msgid "Using AI as a spellchecker or grammar helper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:83
msgid "Using it to help with translation into English"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:84
msgid "Using it to help outline and organize a draft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:85
msgid "Using it adversarially, to point out missing sections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:86
msgid "Ensuring formatting adheres to our style guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:88
msgid ""
"We want to be open and transparent with our users about the way in which AI "
"is or is not used in the our documentation. We (the maintainers) have been "
"experimenting with the ways in which AI can be used to improve the "
"experience for our readers, and we don't object to contributors doing the "
"same -- with the following caveats:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:90
msgid ""
"**Agreement**: Any such work you do *must* be tied to an issue, and be "
"agreed as valid and necessary with the maintainers *before* you start. Only "
"maintainers are exempt from this rule, since they are most familiar with the "
"project and its scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:92
msgid ""
"**Honesty**: If you use an \"AI assist\" when making a contribution, you "
"*must* disclose that you used it, and how you used it in the pull request "
"description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:94
msgid ""
"**Accessibility**: Issues marked as \"good first issues\" and \"Open "
"Documentation Academy\" are *specifically* created and intended for people "
"new to Open Source to get started in a safe place. These issues are easy to "
"complete, well-described, and self-contained for new contributors to learn "
"from. These issues are not for AI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:96
msgid ""
"**Responsibility**: Make sure that even if you use AI, you are still adding "
"value based on your own personal skills and competency. You must understand "
"what you're submitting, even if you used an LLM to help you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:98
msgid "Publishing and hosting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:100
msgid ""
"The documentation for _snap_ is [hosted in GitHub](https://github.com/"
"canonical/snap-docs) and rendered, via [Read the Docs](https://"
"about.readthedocs.com/), to [https://snapcraft.io/docs/](https://"
"snapcraft.io/docs/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:104
msgid ""
"We use the [Sphinx documentation generator](https://www.sphinx-doc.org/) to "
"create our documentation, which is written in [MyST Markdown](https://"
"mystmd.org/) and built from [Canonical's Sphinx Starter Pack](https://"
"github.com/canonical/sphinx-docs-starter-pack)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:106
msgid ""
"For further details, see the [Sphinx Stack documentation](https://canonical-"
"starter-pack.readthedocs-hosted.com/stable/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:108
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/index.md:110
msgid ""
"Lastly, we would like to thank you for spending your time to help make the "
"SnapD documentation better. Every step in the right direction is a step "
"worth taking, no matter how large or small."
msgstr ""
